'''Zabraks''' were a [[near-human]] [[Diet|carnivorous]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]]s [[Iridonia]] and [[Dathomir]]. Most members of the species had distinctive horns atop their heads, as well as two [[heart]]s. Although [[Iridonian|most]] Zabraks lived on Iridonia, [[Dathomirian|some]] settled on the planet [[Dathomir]], where the [[Gender|females]] of the species, known as [[Nightsisters]], ruled over the [[Nightbrothers|Nightbrother]] males and practiced powerful [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] [[magick]]. Notably, female Dathomirian Zabraks had paler skin and lacked the cranial horns shared by the rest of the species.

Zabraks fought against the [[Galactic Empire]]'s attempts to undermine and subvert them, and instead of surrendering, many joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Zabraks were considered to be proud, self-determined, and even arrogant to some, and they were one of the most independent species in [[the galaxy]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Zabraks are too chewy.|[[Deva Lompop]]|<ref name="Jabba the Hutt">[[War of the Bounty Hunters – Jabba the Hutt 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters – Jabba the Hutt'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:EethKothSkeleton-TCWs2BR.png|thumb|left|220px|The skeletal structure of Zabrak Jedi Master Eeth Koth]]
Zabraks were a [[species]] of [[near-human]]s that had evolved to be tough due to the nature of their [[homeworld]] [[Iridonia]]. The species was [[Diet|carnivorous]] and had two [[heart]]s, which allowed them to pump [[oxygen]]ated [[blood]] around their systems more quickly than other species meaning they could go faster for longer. Some Zabraks possessed a ring of small,<ref name="HelmetCollection">{{HelmetCollectionCite|79|Databank A-Z}}</ref> vestigial horns<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> that ran from high on their brow round to the back of their head. The horns of [[Gender|males]] were generally more developed than those of females, although horn placement, length, and thickness varied enormously across the species. Zabraks could be [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="HelmetCollection" />

There were two subspecies of Zabraks, the [[Dathomirian]]s and the [[Iridonian]]s.<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> Female Dathomirians did not have any horns, but males did.<ref name="Monster" />

==Society and culture==
All Zabraks were fiercely independent, usually taking on roles in society that minimized their need to be ordered around by others. This was often mistaken by other species for aloofness or arrogance, which was erroneous, although Zabraks were unashamedly proud of being survivors. The majority of Zabraks wore facial [[tattoo]]s which often indicated familial ties, but could also simply be based on an individual's personal taste.<ref name="HelmetCollection" /> They were a colonial species, having migrated and adapted to dominate many worlds. The Zabraks of [[Iridonia]] were commonly seen traveling across [[the galaxy]] as [[Jedi]], [[bounty hunter]]s, or in other professions. A group of tribal male Zabraks lived on the [[planet]] [[Dathomir]], where they were subservient to the female [[Nightsisters]], but dwelt separately from them. Much of the Dathomirian Zabraks' culture was unknown to outsiders, as they did not trust offworlders.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==History==
The Zabraks were loyal members of the [[Galactic Republic]] during its [[Republic Era|reign]], but were immediately opposed to the [[Galactic Empire]] upon its [[Proclamation of the New Order|creation]], with many joining the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Likewise, many Zabraks sided with the [[Resistance]] to oppose the [[First Order]] after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|fall]] of the [[New Republic]].<ref name="HelmetCollection" />

==Zabraks in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Ah&mdash;is that a fellow ''Zabrak'' I see? And a Nightb&mdash;''"<br />"''You do not know me.|A [[Unidentified Zabrak bartender's father|Zabrak bartender]] and Darth Maul|<ref name="Darth Maul 2">[[Darth Maul (2017) 2|''Darth Maul'' (2017) 2]]</ref>}}
[[File:DarthMaul-SWTLC.png|thumb|right|220px|Darth Maul, a Dathomirian Zabrak Sith Lord.]]
Despite the species overall loyalty to the Republic, individual Zabraks could be found across [[the galaxy]] with a wide range of allegiances, usually in roles with minimal managerial supervision such as independent traders, [[Mercenary|mercenaries]], [[bounty hunter]]s, or [[scout]]s. One such Zabrak was [[Sugi (bounty hunter)|Sugi]], who worked as a bounty hunter during the [[Clone Wars]], and taught her niece [[Jas Emari]] the same trade. Another was a member of the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] on the [[planet]] [[Nevarro]]. Criminal pursuits were often attractive to younger Zabraks, and during the [[Iron Blockade]] of the [[Anoat sector]] several Zabraks served in the crew of the [[the Smuggler]], who led the [[Uprising]] against the Imperial [[blockade]].<ref name="HelmetCollection2">{{HelmetCollectionCite|79|Databank A-Z}}</ref> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> members of the species could be seen on planets such as [[Sorgan]]<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref> and an<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> [[RTK111]],<ref name="AoMS2">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season Two)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Two]]</ref> where a Zabrak worked for gangster [[Gor Koresh]].<ref name="Chapter 9" />

Several [[The Force|Force]]-sensitive Zabraks joined the [[Jedi Order]] during the time of the Galactic Republic, including [[Zubain Ankonori]], [[Eeth Koth]], and [[Agen Kolar]], the latter two of whom served time on the [[Jedi High Council]]. Conversely, the Force-sensitive brothers [[Maul]] and [[Savage Opress]] both served the [[Sith]] before independently forming the [[Shadow Collective]] criminal cartel and briefly ruling the planet [[Mandalore]].<ref name="HelmetCollection2" /> A number of Dathomirian Zabraks lived on [[Dathomir]], the world for which their race was named, as the [[Nightbrothers]], who existed under the rule of the Dathomirian [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] witch clan.<ref name="Monster" />

